BLOAD - load a raw file to memory››Syntax:› BLOAD [d:][path]file[.ext]›       [[$]bank:][$]address››Reads the whole file, unchanged, into›memory from the given address, then›returns to DOS. A bank index before›the colon loads into extended memory.›Nothing is checked: the file may›overwrite anything.››Numbers are decimal; a leading $ means›hex.››Example:› BLOAD FONT.FNT $9C00››See also: LOAD, SAVE, MDUMP›